  "claim": "The Taoiseach of LÉ Ciara (P42) held the position of Taoiseach of Dublin when he dissolved the list of members who were elected to the lower house of the Oireachtas of Ireland on 25 May 1989.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Members of the 25th Dáil. Sentence: The 25th Dáil was dissolved by President Patrick Hillery, at the request of the Taoiseach Charles Haughey on 25 May 1989.\nPage: Charles Haughey. Sentence: Charles James Haughey (16 September 1925 – 13 June 2006) was Taoiseach of Ireland, serving three terms in office (from December 1979 to June 1981, March 1982 to December 1982, and March 1987 to February 1992).\nPage: LÉ Ciara (P42). Sentence: She passed to the Irish Naval Service in 1988 and was commissioned under her current name by the then Taoiseach Charles Haughey on 16 January 1989.",
  "evidence_text": "Page: Members of the 25th Dáil. Sentence: The 25th Dáil was dissolved by President Patrick Hillery, at the request of the Taoiseach Charles Haughey on 25 May 1989.\nPage: Charles Haughey. Sentence: Charles James Haughey (16 September 1925 – 13 June 2006) was Taoiseach of Ireland, serving three terms in office (from December 1979 to June 1981, March 1982 to December 1982, and March 1987 to February 1992).\nPage: LÉ Ciara (P42). Sentence: She passed to the Irish Naval Service in 1988 and was commissioned under her current name by the then Taoiseach Charles Haughey on 16 January 1989.",
