        "original_id": "99c9fe30-3a1e-52b7-82bd-d88f14f4b795",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Roles: Taoiseach\n- Places: Dublin, Ireland\n- Organizations: Oireachtas of Ireland\n- Events: 1989 Irish lower-house election process\n- Concepts: dissolution of elected members list\n\nFacts:\n- On 25 May 1989, the list of members elected to the lower house of the Oireachtas of Ireland was dissolved.\n- The officeholder associated with LÉ Ciara (P42) held the role of Taoiseach when that dissolution occurred.\n- At that time, the Taoiseach was described as holding the position of Taoiseach of Dublin.",
