        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "e52f4674-7603-5c3a-9bde-c863708ff71a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Charles Haughey, Patrick Hillery\n- Organizations: Irish Naval Service\n- Products: LÉ Ciara (P42)\n- Events: 25th Dáil dissolution, LÉ Ciara commissioning\n- Roles: Taoiseach of Ireland, President of Ireland\n\nFacts:\n- Charles Haughey served as Taoiseach of Ireland from December 1979 to June 1981, from March 1982 to December 1982, and from March 1987 to February 1992.\n- LÉ Ciara passed to the Irish Naval Service in 1988.\n- Charles Haughey, then Taoiseach, commissioned LÉ Ciara under her current name on 16 January 1989.\n- President Patrick Hillery dissolved the 25th Dáil on 25 May 1989 at the request of Taoiseach Charles Haughey.",
